<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Yongfu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a>–<a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Yongfu was a Chinese soldier and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-flag-army">Black Flag Army</a>, which fought the French in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the 1870s and 1880s. In 1895, when the Qing ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, he joined the short-lived Republic of Formosa and became its leader after President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-jingsong">Tang Jingsong</a> fled, continuing resistance from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tainan">Tainan</a> until he too fled to the mainland in October 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-yongfu.jpg" alt="Liu Yongfu" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liu_Yongfu_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
